        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**The class series OVERLAP — never stack them.** `io-wait` runs on the reaper thread concurrently with the decode thread, so it routinely exceeds 100% of wall; that is the streaming design working, not an error. Only the **phase** row (`route`/`moe`/`tail`) partitions wall and may be stacked.\n\n**`gpu-wait` is not GPU utilisation.** It is the host blocked in a device join. Measured against `rocm-smi`, gpu-wait reads ~95% of wall while the device is ~84% busy — the ~11-point gap is launch/queue-drain overhead.\n\nNo residual is reported anywhere: unattributed time is absent rather than folded into a bucket. See `docs/measurement/how-to-measure.md`.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.3.1",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "type": "text"
    },
